{"bill":{"id":"119-sres-492","congress":119,"billType":"sres","billNumber":"492","title":"A resolution recognizing community care as an essential tool for meeting the health care needs of the veterans of the United States.","introducedDate":"2025-11-10","latestActionDate":"2025-12-17","latestActionText":"Resolution agreed to in Senate without amendment and with a preamble by Unanimous Consent. (consideration: CR S8874; text: CR S8874)","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","subjects":["Community life and organization","Health facilities and institutions","Public-private cooperation","Veterans' medical care"],"sponsorBioguideId":"B001243","cosponsorBioguideIds":["C001096","T000476","W000437","M000934"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"This resolution recognizes the necessity of community care for veterans and affirms that it complements the mission of the Department of Veterans Affairs (VA). The resolution urges the VA to implement the letter and spirit of the VA Mission Act of 2018, which establishes the Veterans Community Care Program, to ensure veterans have timely access to community providers when the VA cannot meet their needs. Further, the resolution reaffirms the commitment of the Senate to timely, quality, affordable, veteran-centered care.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-resolution/492","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/sres/BILLSTATUS-119sres492.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:30:52.499Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-sres-492","plainSummary":"This resolution is a non-binding statement recognizing that community care—health services provided by private providers outside the VA system—is an important way to meet veterans' health needs. It urges the Department of Veterans Affairs to fully implement the 2018 law that created the Veterans Community Care Program, ensuring veterans can access private providers when the VA cannot serve them in a timely manner. The resolution does not change law or create new programs; it expresses the Senate's support for existing community-care arrangements.","industries":[{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"The resolution emphasizes community care, which directs veterans to private hospitals and physician groups when VA facilities cannot meet demand."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"50c5e1cfdff41c3ee4737608","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:37:46.166Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This resolution would recognize the necessity of community care for veterans and affirms that it complements the mission of the VA.","whoItTouches":"Veterans and their families.","everydayEffect":"If it passed, the change would show up in what the VA does for you. Nothing has changed yet. This kind of resolution does not become law, even if it passes.","confidence":"crs-summary","source":"Reworded from the official summary. Staff at the Congressional Research Service wrote that summary. It is public domain, and the full text of it is further down this page.","titleInPlainWords":null},"overlaps":[{"billId":"119-sres-492","bioguideId":"T000476","cycle":2026,"score":0.022257305757395988,"matches":[{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":69000,"donorShare":0.022257305757395988,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.022257305757395988}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.6617669078945723},"member":{"name":"Thom Tillis","chamber":"Senate","state":"NC","imageUrl":"data/portraits/T000476.jpg","role":"Cosponsor"},"donorProfile":{"bioguideId":"T000476","cycle":2026,"totalItemized":3100105.6799999997,"byIndustry":[{"industry":"finance-banking","amount":190800,"share":0.0615462889